    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey so my monstera deliciosa has been acting weird lately. some of the older leaves are turning a weird yellowish color and they feel kind of soft. i dont want it to die, any idea what's going on? i live in seattle so it's pretty cloudy here all the time",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yellowing and soft older leaves on your Monstera deliciosa, especially in a cloudy Seattle environment, could be a sign of a few things, like overwatering or nutrient deficiencies. It's very common for tropical plants to suffer when their environment isn't perfectly matched to their needs, and your plant might be stressed by the lack of direct, bright light. Try to check the soil moisture; if it's soggy, let it dry out more between waterings, which is a common issue with indoor plants. You might also consider a gentle fertilizer boost if you haven't fed it recently.",
